  READING.
  * dim = 0 for all J <= 3, every D:  on Session 18's polynomial locus
    (J = 0) and on every weaker relaxation the endgame system has ONLY
    the zero solution.  The obstruction is universal in the chain
    degree -- it is not special to D = 13.
  * dim jumps 0 -> 1 at J = 4 for every D, and the new direction
    carries c != 0 except at D = 3, 6, 9, 12.
  * a SECOND jump 1 -> 2 appears at J = D/3 whenever 3 | D and
    D/3 >= 5.  That is a resonance of the homogeneous operator, and it
    is Jacobian-silent (see probe 2b).
  * at D = 3, 6, 9, 12 the resonance sits at J = D/3 <= 4, i.e. it
    collides with the unlocking direction and absorbs it: those four
    chain degrees are rigid at every pole order.

